1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,060
In 2022, a glacial lake flood in Hunza

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,090
destroyed a Karakoram Highway bridge.

3
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:10,374
Pakistan watches these lakes with optical satellites.

4
00:00:10,414 --> 00:00:14,350
In July, SUPARCO said cloud made changes hard to assess.

5
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:17,780
At Attabad, cloud covers the optical view.

6
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:21,960
NASA and ISRO's NISAR radar sees the lake through it.

7
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:25,695
We're SARcastic Scientists from Islamabad,

8
00:00:25,735 --> 00:00:27,458
and we built SARtale.

9
00:00:27,498 --> 00:00:29,940
Open Lake Watch, and pick Passu.

10
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:33,084
Each NISAR pass estimates the water

11
00:00:33,124 --> 00:00:35,200
area inside the lake's outline.

12
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:38,084
SARtale compares it with the lake's

13
00:00:38,124 --> 00:00:40,270
own earlier passes on the same track,

14
00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:42,690
and shows the whole history.

15
00:00:43,530 --> 00:00:46,366
Passu's flag began with a processing update,

16
00:00:46,406 --> 00:00:49,760
so it needs checking before anyone calls it a change.

17
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:52,509
Anyone can request another lake,

18
00:00:52,549 --> 00:00:54,450
and the data refreshes weekly.

19
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:57,700
When clouds close in, the lakes stay in view.
